    "body": "# Description\n\n`docs/support_matrix.rst` does not list compute capability 11.0 (Jetson AGX Thor). Footnote 3 also says MXFP8 is limited to 10.x, but `_compute_mxfp8_support()` in `transformer_engine/pytorch/quantization.py` enables it from 10.0 up to, but not including, 12.0, which includes 11.0.\n\nThis follows up on #2556, where I posted a full L0 run on Jetson AGX Thor: https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/issues/2556#issuecomment-6219259028\n\n**Depends on #3706.** The 11.0 NVFP4 cell says \"Yes\" because stochastic rounding in the RHT cast-fusion kernels works on 11.0 only with that fix. Without it, the default NVFP4 recipe returns all-zero wgrad on 11.0. If #3706 does not land, that cell should be \"Partial\" with a footnote like the one for 12.x.\n\n## Type of change\n\n- [x] Documentation change (change only to the documentation, either a fix or a new content)\n- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)\n- [ ] Infra/Build change\n- [ ] Code refactoring\n\n## Changes\n\n- Compute capability table: add 11.0, Blackwell (Jetson), Jetson AGX Thor.\n- Format table: add 11.0 with BF16, FP8 (per tensor), FP8 block scaling, MXFP8 and NVFP4 all \"Yes\".\n- Footnote 3: MXFP8 is supported on 10.0 through 11.x.\n- Footnote 4: the full NVFP4 recipe is supported on 10.x and 11.0.\n- Default recipe table: 11.0 uses `MXFP8BlockScaling`.\n\n## Basis\n\nJetson AGX Thor, JetPack 7.2, CUDA 13.2, cuDNN 9.20, TE built from source with `NVTE_CUDA_ARCHS=110`.\n\n- `is_fp8_available()`, `is_fp8_block_scaling_available()`, `is_mxfp8_available()` and `is_nvfp4_available()` all return `True`, and `get_default_fp8_recipe()` returns `MXFP8BlockScaling`.\n- In the L0 PyTorch run linked above, the FP8, FP8 block-scaling and MXFP8 quantization and GEMM suites pass (for example `test_mxfp8`: 447 passed, 0 failed). Other MXFP8-related failures fall into two groups. Four are attention tests: MXFP8 FusedAttention needs cuDNN 9.21 or newer on any architecture, and JetPack 7.2 ships 9.20. Two are `test_grouped_mlp` cases for the CuTeDSL fused grouped MLP. TE enables that path only on 10.x, and its cuDNN-frontend kernel uses `redux.f32`, which `sm_110a` lacks (NVIDIA/cudnn-frontend#1686). Neither affects the recipe-level support this table describes.\n- `tests/pytorch/nvfp4`: 9314 passed, 0 failed with #3706; 15 failed without it.\n\nI did not build the Sphinx docs. The change adds table rows in the existing format and edits two footnotes.\n\n# Checklist:\n\n- [x] I have read and followed the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.rst)\n- [x] The functionality is complete\n- [ ] I have commented my code, particularly in hard-to-understand areas (n/a)\n- [x] I have made corresponding changes to the documentation\n- [x] My changes generate no new warnings\n- [ ] I have added tests that prove my fix is effective or that my feature works (n/a, docs only)\n- [ ] New and existing unit tests pass locally with my changes (n/a, docs only)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
